<TD class="left"><sup>3</sup>⁄<sub>4</sub> cup.</TD>
</TR>
<TR>
<TD class="left border-right-single">Fruits <sup>5</sup></TD>
<TD class="left"><sup>3</sup>⁄<sub>4</sub> cup.</TD>
</TR>
<TR>
<TD class="left border-bottom-single border-right-single">Grains <sup>6</sup></TD>
<TD class="left border-bottom-single">1 ounce equivalent.
</TD>
</TR>
</TBODY>
<TFOOT><TR><TD colspan="2"><sup>1</sup> Must serve two of the five components for a reimbursable afterschool snack. Only one of the two components may be a beverage.
</TD></TR><TR><TD colspan="2"><sup>2</sup> May need to serve larger portions to children ages 13 through 18 to meet their nutritional needs.
</TD></TR><TR><TD colspan="2"><sup>3</sup> Must be fat-free (skim) or low-fat (1 percent fat or less). Milk may be unflavored or flavored.
</TD></TR><TR><TD colspan="2"><sup>4</sup> Alternate protein products must meet the requirements in appendix A to part 226 of this chapter. Yogurt must contain no more than 12 grams of added sugars per 6 ounces (2 grams of added sugars per ounce). Information on crediting meats/meat alternates may be found in FNS guidance.
